basisu: Accumulate the ETC1 optimizer's average colour in double

Applies to: KTX-Software v5.0.0-rc2 (vendored basis_universal, lib version 210),
            from the source root: `git apply <this file>`.
Fixes:      educelab/preppy#5 (from educelab/dri-voyager#13).

etc1_optimizer::init sums a cluster's pixel colours into a float32 vec3F. Past
2^32 the spacing between float32 values exceeds 510, so adding a pixel of 255 no
longer changes the sum. For a large bright ETC1S endpoint cluster (more than about
16.8M pixels of 255; ETC1S shares one codebook across all mip levels, so this
happens on 8K textures with large clipped-white areas) the average comes out far
too dark. Example: PHerc1166Cr01 IR1050 FE2's white cluster averages 148.97
instead of 254.95. The cluster then gets an endpoint that can't represent white,
and the encoded texture shows flat grey blocks in some mip levels.

Summing in double fixes it. With this patch, at the default --clevel 1, that
cluster gets base 255 / table 0 and every mip level encodes cleanly.

Upstream:   https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal/issues/476
            https://github.com/KhronosGroup/KTX-Software/issues/1324

Drop this patch when a KTX-Software release vendors a basis_universal with the
accumulation fixed (as of 2026-11, basis_universal master still sums in float32).

diff --git a/external/basis_universal/encoder/basisu_etc.cpp b/external/basis_universal/encoder/basisu_etc.cpp
index 5bae228..1a68084 100644
--- a/external/basis_universal/encoder/basisu_etc.cpp
+++ b/external/basis_universal/encoder/basisu_etc.cpp
@@ -1010,7 +1010,9 @@ namespace basisu
 
 		m_limit = m_pParams->m_use_color4 ? 15 : 31;
 
-		vec3F avg_color(0.0f);
+		// Accumulate in double: a float32 sum stops growing past 2^32, so the average
+		// of a large bright cluster (> ~16.8M pixels of 255) comes out far too dark.
+		double sum_r = 0, sum_g = 0, sum_b = 0;
 
 		m_luma.resize(n);
 		m_sorted_luma_indices.resize(n);
@@ -1031,14 +1033,14 @@ namespace basisu
 			max_g = basisu::maximum<int>(max_g, c.g);
 			max_b = basisu::maximum<int>(max_b, c.b);
 
-			const vec3F fc(c.r, c.g, c.b);
-
-			avg_color += fc;
+			sum_r += c.r;
+			sum_g += c.g;
+			sum_b += c.b;
 
 			m_luma[i] = static_cast<uint16_t>(c.r + c.g + c.b);
 			m_sorted_luma_indices[i] = i;
 		}
-		avg_color /= static_cast<float>(n);
+		const vec3F avg_color((float)(sum_r / n), (float)(sum_g / n), (float)(sum_b / n));
 		m_avg_color = avg_color;
 		m_max_comp_spread = basisu::maximum(basisu::maximum(max_r - min_r, max_g - min_g), max_b - min_b);
 
